; color-soundsystem — a dub sound system in the bus garage, built from the desk's tools:
; the skank sliced in time and its echo spread wide, the mixer's kills on the faders,
; the Leslie, and the limiter at the end of the night

the bus garage
--------------
; fader1 kills and lifts the lows, fader2 the highs (0.5 is flat), fader3 the kick's attack,
; fader4 the echo's feedback. The skank only speaks on the offbeat, and its echo is spread wide
; while the drums and the bass stay in the middle
the clock is clock 4
the kick is kick samplerate=half
the chords is chord 4 samplerate=quarter
the skank is slicer pattern=offbeat len=0.5 samplerate=half
the pedal is drive type=od drive=0.3 tone=0.6 samplerate=half
the echo is delay 6 feedback=0.5 samplerate=half   ; a darker echo, and half the work
the air is widener width=0.9 samplerate=half
the punch is transient samplerate=half
the desk is eq samplerate=half
the wall is limiter ceiling=0.85 samplerate=half

clock.beat -> kick.strike
clock.eighth -> skank.clock
chords -> skank -> pedal -> echo -> air
kick -> punch -> desk -> wall
pedal -40> wall
fader1 -> desk.low
fader2 -> desk.high
fader3 -> punch.attack
fader4 -> echo.feedback
wall -> left right leds
air.left -60> left
air.right -60> right

the organ in the back room
--------------------------
; a chord through the Leslie: hold PLAY for fast, let go and the drum takes its time to slow.
; fader1 how hard the valve amp is pushed, fader2 the tremolo on the bass
the clock is clock 3
the organ is chord 4 type=0.6
the amp is drive type=crunch samplerate=half
the leslie is rotary
the bass is vco 1
the throb is tremolo type=harmonic stereo=on shape=0.4
the wall is limiter ceiling=0.8

play -> leslie.fast
organ -> amp -> leslie
fader1 -> amp.drive
bass.sine -> throb
fader2 -> throb.depth
leslie.left -> left
leslie.right -> right
throb.left -50> left
throb.right -50> right
